From: fpvOS contributors <dev@fpvos.local>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: add the Ascent 60 Hz profile

Document the opt-in 720p60/1080p60 board profile and matching LT9611
calibration quirk. Preserve the existing 1080p-only profile.

Upstream: not submitted
Signed-off-by: fpvOS contributors <dev@fpvos.local>

---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/artosyn,ar9311-vo.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/artosyn,ar9311-vo.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/artosyn,ar9311-vo.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/artosyn,ar9311-vo.yaml
@@ -14,6 +14,8 @@
   supported fixed display profile and supply their board output graph.
   The ascent-1080p60 profile preserves the validated Ascent raster, divider
   and four-lane RGB888 DSI sync-event PHY setup for CEA-16 at 148.5 MHz.
+  The ascent-60hz profile also supports CEA-4 1280x720p60 at 74.25 MHz,
+  using the same lane clock and longer internal blanking.
   It relies on early firmware clock and pinmux setup; it does not describe
   arbitrary modes or guarantee compatibility with another board's sink.
 
@@ -26,7 +28,7 @@
 
   artosyn,display-profile:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string
-    const: ascent-1080p60
+    enum: [ascent-1080p60, ascent-60hz]
     description: Explicit selection of the supported fixed output setup.
 
   reg-names:
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/artosyn,ar9311-dsi.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/artosyn,ar9311-dsi.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/artosyn,ar9311-dsi.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/artosyn,ar9311-dsi.yaml
@@ -14,6 +14,8 @@
   supported fixed display profile and supply their board output graph.
   The ascent-1080p60 profile preserves the validated Ascent raster, divider
   and four-lane RGB888 DSI sync-event PHY setup for CEA-16 at 148.5 MHz.
+  The ascent-60hz profile also supports CEA-4 1280x720p60 at 74.25 MHz,
+  using the same lane clock and longer internal blanking.
   It relies on early firmware clock and pinmux setup; it does not describe
   arbitrary modes or guarantee compatibility with another board's sink.
 
@@ -26,7 +28,7 @@
 
   artosyn,display-profile:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string
-    const: ascent-1080p60
+    enum: [ascent-1080p60, ascent-60hz]
     description: Explicit selection of the supported fixed output setup.
 
   clocks:
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/bridge/lontium,lt9611.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/bridge/lontium,lt9611.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/bridge/lontium,lt9611.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/bridge/lontium,lt9611.yaml
@@ -34,6 +34,14 @@
       The page selector can read back stale register data. Cache only the
       selector so every page change is written explicitly; data registers
       remain volatile. Select this only on hardware with this behavior.
+
+  lontium,ascent-60hz-quirk:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      Use Ascent fixed-M calibration and clock-recovery reset after TMDS enable.
+      Supports RGB CEA-4 720p60 and CEA-16 1080p60 only, with the matching
+      Artosyn ascent-60hz DSI raster profile. Programs the corresponding AVI
+      packet and PCR multiplier. DVI and audio are not supported.
 
   lontium,fixed-1080p60-quirk:
     type: boolean
